{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "16", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "33", "S": "49"}}, "news": [{"title": "Mohali: Consumer forum orders PUDA to refund \u20b914.5 lakh with interest", "para": "The District Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission-II mandated PUDA to refund \u20b914.5 lakh to Gurdeep Singh. Singh received an unfeasible plot in the Gateway City project in Mohali. The commission found PUDA guilty of unfair trade practice for not providing possession on time. Singh had acquired rights from a previous allottee and requested a refund citing the plot's marshy condition.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/mohali-consumer-forum-orders-puda-to-refund-14-5-lakh-with-interest/134982196?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-103/134982196.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Gurugram civic body flags 87 unsafe buildings, set to raze them", "para": "In a proactive move to safeguard its residents, Gurgaon's civic body has pinpointed 87 hazardous buildings slated for demolition. The recent inspection unveiled alarming structural issues such as cracks and tilting. While show-cause notices have been dispatched to the owners of 66 structures, the action is still in process for the remaining ones.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/gurugram-civic-body-flags-87-unsafe-buildings-set-to-raze-them/134982160?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-284560/134982160.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Pune development body tightens water norms for building, occupancy approvals", "para": "The Pune Metropolitan Region Development Authority has introduced a new requirement for developers: an assured water supply must now be obtained for building permissions. This revision seeks to enhance the reliability of water availability and supersedes earlier rules, affecting various types of developments. Developers of new residential and commercial projects must adhere to these updated standards to address community concerns over inadequate water supply in burgeoning areas.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/pune-development-body-tightens-water-norms-for-building-occupancy-approvals/134981997?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-335706/134981997.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}